WEBVTT

00:00.116 --> 00:02.353
Turn a ninety-degree corner in this car,

00:02.353 --> 00:04.259
and the outside back wheel rolls about

00:04.259 --> 00:06.076
eight feet farther than the inside wheel.

00:06.276 --> 00:07.776
One engine drives both.

00:08.056 --> 00:08.976
So who's cheating?

00:09.817 --> 00:11.237
Tight turn or lazy one,

00:11.357 --> 00:12.877
if both turn through ninety degrees,

00:13.137 --> 00:14.237
it's the same eight feet.

00:14.477 --> 00:15.757
The wider apart the wheels,

00:15.917 --> 00:17.257
the bigger that gap.

00:18.117 --> 00:19.848
Bolt them to one solid axle,

00:19.848 --> 00:20.883
and a tire has

00:20.883 --> 00:21.877
to skid the difference.

00:22.257 --> 00:23.777
Go-karts just live with that.

00:24.683 --> 00:26.483
So your car has this instead.

00:26.783 --> 00:28.863
The drive shaft spins a small gear,

00:28.863 --> 00:30.023
and that turns a big one,

00:30.163 --> 00:30.903
the ring gear,

00:31.043 --> 00:32.863
which carries a little cage of gears.

00:33.717 --> 00:35.457
Each wheel's axle ends in a gear,

00:35.457 --> 00:37.137
with two small gears in between.

00:37.477 --> 00:37.977
Going straight,

00:38.077 --> 00:39.317
they ride along without spinning.

00:39.597 --> 00:40.917
Easiest job in the car.

00:41.717 --> 00:42.463
Then you turn,

00:42.463 --> 00:43.897
and the inside wheel slows.

00:44.197 --> 00:45.697
The small gears start to spin,

00:45.817 --> 00:47.097
and whatever speed it loses,

00:47.297 --> 00:48.397
the outside wheel gains.

00:48.697 --> 00:49.697
In our tight turn,

00:49.857 --> 00:51.357
that's thirteen percent each way.

00:52.188 --> 00:52.988
The catch is that

00:52.988 --> 00:53.968
it's fair with torque.

00:54.128 --> 00:54.688
Too fair.

00:54.948 --> 00:56.088
Put one wheel on ice,

00:56.208 --> 00:57.928
and the dry one only gets the

00:57.928 --> 00:59.468
tiny twist the ice can hold.

00:59.708 --> 01:01.728
The icy one spins at double speed,

01:01.888 --> 01:03.828
and you go nowhere, loudly.

01:04.867 --> 01:06.496
That's what limited-slip diffs

01:06.496 --> 01:07.607
and lockers are for.

01:07.827 --> 01:08.787
They let the wheel

01:08.787 --> 01:09.907
with grip take more,

01:10.087 --> 01:11.201
the one time you want

01:11.201 --> 01:12.547
your car to play favorites.
